<https://archive.org/details/Fsi-GermanBasicCourse-StudentText>
    dcterms:title "German Basic Course, Units 1–12 (Foreign Service Institute, 1961), volume 1 as scanned on the Internet Archive" ;
    dcterms:creator "Samuel A. Brown and the German staff of the Foreign Service Institute, U.S. Department of State" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "A work of the United States Government: the title page reads \"Foreign Service Institute, Department of State … Washington, D.C. 1961\" and the preface says the course \"has been designed to assist United States Government representatives\" and \"has benefited from the labors of many members and former members of the FSI staff. In its present form it was prepared under the supervision of Dr. Samuel A. Brown\". 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\". The Internet Archive item's metadata (https://archive.org/metadata/Fsi-GermanBasicCourse-StudentText) gives licenseurl \"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/publicdomain/\". Recorded here with the Public Domain Mark: free of known copyright."@en .

<https://archive.org/details/GermanPhraseBook>
    dcterms:title "German Phrase Book, TM 30-606 (War Department, 30 November 1943), as scanned on the Internet Archive" ;
    dcterms:creator "United States War Department" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/> ;
    rdfs:comment "A work of the United States Government: the cover reads \"German Phrase Book … War Department, Washington, November 30, 1943\", and the page after it \"TM 30-606, German Phrase Book, is published for military personnel only, and is not to be republished in whole or in part without the consent of the War Department. … By order of the Secretary of War: G. C. Marshall, Chief of Staff.\" 17 U.S.C. § 105 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/17/105): \"Copyright protection under this title is not available for any work of the United States Government\". The republication notice and the cover marking \"RESTRICTED\" are a wartime War Department distribution instruction, not a claim of copyright; the booklet is published openly by the Internet Archive (metadata https://archive.org/metadata/GermanPhraseBook, which states no licence). Recorded here with the Public Domain Mark: free of known copyright."@en .

